1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,037
If God knew

2
00:00:01,057 --> 00:00:02,176
Samson would throw

3
00:00:02,196 --> 00:00:03,436
it all away,

4
00:00:03,456 --> 00:00:04,645
why did He give

5
00:00:04,665 --> 00:00:06,079
him so much strength?

6
00:00:06,099 --> 00:00:07,068
He knew Samson

7
00:00:07,088 --> 00:00:07,593
would chase

8
00:00:07,613 --> 00:00:08,784
a Philistine wife

9
00:00:08,804 --> 00:00:10,160
his parents didn't want.

10
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:11,149
He knew Samson

11
00:00:11,169 --> 00:00:12,340
would tell Delilah

12
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:13,127
how to take

13
00:00:13,147 --> 00:00:14,241
his strength away.

14
00:00:14,261 --> 00:00:15,430
And still He gave

15
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:16,321
him the strength

16
00:00:16,341 --> 00:00:16,915
to tear

17
00:00:16,935 --> 00:00:18,034
a lion apart

18
00:00:18,054 --> 00:00:18,925
and strike down

19
00:00:18,945 --> 00:00:20,045
a thousand men

20
00:00:20,065 --> 00:00:21,390
with a jawbone.

21
00:00:21,410 --> 00:00:21,966
The clue

22
00:00:21,986 --> 00:00:23,340
is what the angel

23
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,204
of the LORD

24
00:00:24,224 --> 00:00:25,290
told his mother

25
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:26,789
before he was born.

26
00:00:26,809 --> 00:00:27,824
"He shall begin

27
00:00:27,844 --> 00:00:28,859
to save Israel

28
00:00:28,879 --> 00:00:29,683
from the hand

29
00:00:29,703 --> 00:00:31,386
of the Philistines."

30
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:32,281
But notice:

31
00:00:32,301 --> 00:00:33,121
it doesn't say

32
00:00:33,141 --> 00:00:34,296
he'll save Israel.

33
00:00:34,316 --> 00:00:34,856
It says

34
00:00:34,876 --> 00:00:36,037
he'll begin to.

35
00:00:36,057 --> 00:00:37,372
Which means Samson's job

36
00:00:37,392 --> 00:00:38,212
was to start

37
00:00:38,232 --> 00:00:38,892
the fight.

38
00:00:38,912 --> 00:00:40,567
Israel wasn't fighting back.

39
00:00:40,587 --> 00:00:41,941
Even his own people

40
00:00:41,961 --> 00:00:42,684
tied him up

41
00:00:42,704 --> 00:00:43,867
to hand him over

42
00:00:43,887 --> 00:00:45,308
to the Philistines.

43
00:00:45,328 --> 00:00:46,371
And that wife?

44
00:00:46,391 --> 00:00:47,315
It sounds wrong

45
00:00:47,335 --> 00:00:48,064
to us,

46
00:00:48,084 --> 00:00:49,564
but the marriage was

47
00:00:49,584 --> 00:00:50,947
part of God's plan.

48
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:51,675
"It was from

49
00:00:51,695 --> 00:00:52,281
the LORD,

50
00:00:52,301 --> 00:00:53,438
for he was seeking

51
00:00:53,458 --> 00:00:54,670
an opportunity

52
00:00:54,690 --> 00:00:56,389
against the Philistines."

53
00:00:56,409 --> 00:00:57,906
Samson wanted a wife.

54
00:00:57,926 --> 00:00:59,108
God wanted to free

55
00:00:59,128 --> 00:01:00,081
His people.

56
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:00,807
So God didn't

57
00:01:00,827 --> 00:01:01,720
give Samson strength

58
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,366
because he deserved it.

59
00:01:03,386 --> 00:01:04,093
He gave it

60
00:01:04,113 --> 00:01:05,930
because Israel needed saving.

61
00:01:05,950 --> 00:01:07,477
Samson's choices cost him

62
00:01:07,497 --> 00:01:08,155
his eyes.

63
00:01:08,175 --> 00:01:09,391
But at the end,

64
00:01:09,411 --> 00:01:10,070
he prayed,

65
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:11,337
"strengthen me only

66
00:01:11,357 --> 00:01:12,140
this once."

67
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,141
God answered,

68
00:01:13,161 --> 00:01:14,080
and the temple

69
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:14,698
came down.

70
00:01:14,718 --> 00:01:16,460
He killed more Philistines

71
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:17,456
in his death than

72
00:01:17,476 --> 00:01:18,769
in his whole life.

73
00:01:18,789 --> 00:01:20,036
Samson started the rescue.

74
00:01:20,056 --> 00:01:21,096
Later, King David

75
00:01:21,116 --> 00:01:22,514
"defeated the Philistines

76
00:01:22,534 --> 00:01:23,639
and subdued them."

77
00:01:23,659 --> 00:01:24,958
And the New Testament

78
00:01:24,978 --> 00:01:25,855
still lists Samson

79
00:01:25,875 --> 00:01:27,061
among the faithful.

80
00:01:27,081 --> 00:01:28,300
So why give Samson

81
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,199
so much strength?

82
00:01:29,219 --> 00:01:30,178
Because it wasn't

83
00:01:30,198 --> 00:01:31,217
about Samson.

84
00:01:31,237 --> 00:01:32,196
It was about

85
00:01:32,216 --> 00:01:33,175
the people God

86
00:01:33,195 --> 00:01:34,019
was saving.

87
00:01:34,039 --> 00:01:35,146
So the next time

88
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:35,709
you think

89
00:01:35,729 --> 00:01:36,770
you've messed up

90
00:01:36,790 --> 00:01:37,896
too much for God

91
00:01:37,916 --> 00:01:38,861
to use you…

92
00:01:38,881 --> 00:01:40,594
remember Samson.
